editor.nod_help.chg.extra=<h2>Exemplos chg</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> altera o início do texto ou um padrão. É útil para telefones, códigos, prefixos e tabelas de renumeração.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estrutura:</b> esquerda = o que procurar, direita = nova forma. Use aspas para espaços, vírgulas ou caracteres especiais.</div><details open><summary>Substituir prefixo</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Regra</th><th>Exemplo</th></tr><tr><td>Prefix</td><td><code>chg "01751","07051"</code></td><td><code>0175112345</code> -> <code>0705112345</code></td></tr><tr><td>Dash</td><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><code>01751-12345</code> -> <code>070-5112345</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Padrão com x</summary><p>NOD 2.0: <code>x</code> captura um dígito e o coloca de volta à direita. Espaços e hífens à esquerda são apenas para leitura.</p><pre>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</pre><p><code>01835-1234</code> -> <code>0183-501234</code>.</p></details><details><summary>Erros comuns</summary><ul><li>Coloque regras específicas acima de regras gerais.</li><li>Não esqueça a vírgula.</li><li>Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> para tradução de valor completo.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.math.extra=<h2>Math em resumo</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> calcula com <code>ans</code>. Na primeira linha <code>ans</code> é o valor de entrada; nas linhas seguintes é o resultado anterior.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estrutura:</b> escolha primeiro o tipo de cálculo e depois escreva a syntax correta. Para fórmulas grandes, use parênteses ou várias linhas <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>.</div><div class="math-flow"><span class="math-pill">1. Operações básicas</span><span class="math-pill">2. Funções e constantes</span><span class="math-pill">3. Fórmulas complexas</span><span class="math-pill">4. Cálculo: diff, integral, limite</span></div><details open><summary>Operações básicas</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Exemplo</th></tr><tr><td>+</td><td><code>math ans + number</code></td><td><code>math ans + 32</code></td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td><code>math ans - number</code></td><td><code>math ans - 10</code></td></tr><tr><td>*</td><td><code>math ans * factor</code></td><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td></tr><tr><td>/</td><td><code>math ans / factor</code></td><td><code>math ans / 1.95583</code></td></tr></table><pre>Name Euro to cents&#13;&#10;input1 Euro&#13;&#10;input2 Cents&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 100&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Funções e constantes</summary><table><tr><th>Groep</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Nota</th></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td><code>math ans^2</code> or <code>math pow(ans,3)</code></td><td>Square, cube.</td></tr><tr><td>Root</td><td><code>math sqrt(ans)</code></td><td>Can be used inside formulas.</td></tr><tr><td>Pi/e</td><td><code>math pi * ans^2</code><br><code>math e^ans</code></td><td>Circle and exponential.</td></tr><tr><td>Degrees</td><td><code>math sind(ans)</code><br><code>math cosd(ans)</code></td><td>Use <code>sin/cos/tan</code> for radians.</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Fórmulas complexas</summary><p>Use parênteses quando a ordem for importante. Escreva sempre a multiplicação com <code>*</code>.</p><pre>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;math ((ans + 10) * 2) / 3&#13;&#10;math ans * (1 + 0.04)^5</pre><h3>Exemplo: Pitágoras</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Hypotenuse&#13;&#10;input1 Side a&#13;&#10;input2 Side c&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Aqui <code>ans</code> é o lado <code>a</code>; o outro lado fica fixo em <code>5</code>.</p></details><details><summary>Cálculo: diff, integral, limite</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Resultado</th></tr><tr><td>Derivative</td><td><code>math diff ans^2</code></td><td>Inclinação numérica.</td></tr><tr><td>Integral</td><td><code>math integral 0,1 ans^2</code></td><td>Área numérica de 0 a 1.</td></tr><tr><td>Limit</td><td><code>math limit 0 sin(ans)/ans</code></td><td>Aproximação em torno de 0.</td></tr></table></details><h2>Erros comuns</h2><ul><li>Não esqueça <code>ans</code>.</li><li>Use <code>sind</code> para graus.</li><li>Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a> para conversão inversa complexa.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.mode.extra=<h2>Quando usar mode?</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> indica que tipo de arquivo NOD você está criando. Para um conversor normal, geralmente não é necessário.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estrutura:</b> use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> apenas para tipos especiais, como processamento de dados ou resolução de equações.</div><details open><summary>Modes</summary><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Quando</th><th>Comandos</th></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td>Conversor normal</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td>Processamento de dados</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td>Resolver equação</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Exemplo: converter</summary><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Exemplo: equation</summary><pre>Name Solve equation&#13;&#10;mode equation&#13;&#10;given y = 20&#13;&#10;equation y = x * 2&#13;&#10;solve x&#13;&#10;constraint x >= 0&#13;&#10;end</pre></details>
editor.nod_help.trans.extra=<h2>Exemplos trans</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> traduz um valor completo. Use para palavras, códigos fixos, estados, códigos postais e listas curtas.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estrutura:</b> <code>trans "old value","new value"</code>. A entrada completa deve corresponder ao valor à esquerda.</div><details open><summary>Traduzir texto exato</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Regra</th><th>Resultado</th></tr><tr><td>Word</td><td><code>trans "hallo","hello"</code></td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td><code>trans "open","in progress"</code></td><td><code>open</code> -> <code>in progress</code></td></tr><tr><td>Address</td><td><code>trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"</code></td><td>postcode + house number -> address</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>trans / chg</summary><table><tr><th>Comando</th><th>Quando</th><th>Exemplo</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a></td><td>A entrada completa é conhecida exatamente.</td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td><td>Só o início ou o padrão muda.</td><td><code>01751-xxxxx</code> -> <code>070-51xxxxx</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Erros comuns</summary><ul><li>Esquerda é entrada, direita é saída.</li><li>Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> para mudanças parciais.</li><li>Evite traduções duplicadas para a mesma entrada.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.full.classic=<h2>Introdução ao editor NOD</h2><p>O editor NOD é o espaço de trabalho dos conversores. O código fica em cima, os testes em baixo e a pré-visualização à direita mostra rótulos, símbolos, texto introdutório e resultados.</p><h2>Clássico 1.73 e NOD 2.0</h2><table><tr><th>Syscalculator 1.73 / NOD 1.0</th><th>Syscalculator 2.0 / editor NOD</th></tr><tr><td>Arquivos de texto clássicos com <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> e <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a>.</td><td>A mesma base continua compatível com arquivos NOD antigos.</td></tr><tr><td>A posição dos símbolos muitas vezes precisava ser lembrada e testada.</td><td>A pré-visualização mostra imediatamente <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> até <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> era principalmente troca de prefixo.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> continua compatível; NOD 2.0 adiciona padrões com capture <code>x</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>A ajuda vinha principalmente de exemplos.</td><td>O editor oferece sugestões, ajuda com clique direito e páginas de exemplos.</td></tr></table><h2>Sintaxe: visão geral completa do NOD 1.0 e NOD 2.0</h2><p>Esta tabela mostra qual sintaxe vem dos arquivos NOD clássicos e o que foi adicionado no NOD 2.0.</p><table class="syntax-compare"><tr><th>Syntax / feature</th><th>NOD 1.0</th><th>NOD 2.0</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Converter name/title.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:urln"><code>URLN</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Reference/source line remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Labels for input and output.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:result"><code>Result</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:resfou"><code>Resfou</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Result label and error text.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Symbols left/right of input and output; NOD 2.0 shows them in preview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>format #.00</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Number formatting stays the same.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 uses <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> for special file types; normal converters also work without mode.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>For table/field processing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>For solving equations with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Classic calculation with <code>ans</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Richer formulas and functions in NOD 2.0.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Classic prefix replacement keeps working.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>New in NOD 2.0: pattern with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td><code>trans "old","new"</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Exact text translation remains compatible.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Reverse direction of a converter.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 data converters with fields and output construction.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:phoneformat"><code>phoneformat</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Format phone numbers in data/number converters.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:lookup"><code>lookup</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:match"><code>match</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Look up tables or connect values.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:constraint"><code>constraint</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Solve equations with constraints.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:preview"><code>preview</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:backup"><code>backup</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Editor/safety information for NOD 2.0 files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>indoprint ... indoend</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Introduction text remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Closes the NOD file.</td></tr><tr><td>Live preview, suggestions, right-click help</td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>This is editor help, not old runtime syntax.</td></tr></table><h2>O que continua</h2><ul><li>Comandos legíveis por linha.</li><li><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> fecha o arquivo.</li><li>Um conversor simples continua curto.</li></ul><h2>O que é novo</h2><ul><li>Pré-visualização ao vivo e simulador.</li><li>Graph Preview para gráficos de conversores math.</li><li>Sugestões ao digitar.</li><li>Ajuda mais completa por comando.</li><li>Mais exemplos para <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a>, símbolos e <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoprint"><code>indoprint</code></a>.</li></ul>
